# Cursor rules for aurora-zfs-simple

Read AGENTS.md first — it is the maintained orientation document for this repo.
These rules are the short form and deliberately do not restate it, so there is
only one copy to keep current.

## Context

A thin Aurora DX derivative that adds ZFS back. It does not compile ZFS; it
assembles three prebuilt Universal Blue artifacts: the Aurora base, akmods and
akmods-zfs.

Correctness depends on TWO of them agreeing about the kernel version: akmods and
akmods-zfs. The Aurora base is not one of them. kernel-akmods.sh erases Aurora's
kernel outright, so this image legitimately runs a newer kernel than Aurora
stable whenever the akmods stream is ahead. That is the design. Never recommend
a downgrade or a pin because the base image's kernel differs.

## Before changing anything in response to a failing build

Most red builds here are caused upstream, not by this repo. akmods tracks
whatever kernel Fedora ships; akmods-zfs can only advance when OpenZFS supports
that kernel. Compare the ostree.linux label on ghcr.io/ublue-os/akmods and
ghcr.io/ublue-os/akmods-zfs for the release the Containerfile targets — those
two labels, and nothing else, decide it. If they differ, that is the diagnosis;
see AGENTS.md for the commands and the options.

Never loosen the kmod-zfs glob in build_files/zfs.sh or make that install
non-fatal to get past it. A kmod built for a different kernel will not load, and
the failure moves from the build to the boot.

## Code

- Shell only. No package manager, no node_modules, no build step. Do not add one.
- shellcheck -x must produce zero output, informational findings included.
- Shebang and executable bit on anything run by path; the Containerfile and the
  workflows run scripts that way. The exception is tests/lib/, which is sourced
  and carries neither.
- Four-space indent, except ci/write-badges.sh and .claude/hooks/gate-git-diff.sh,
  which are two.
- Run ./tests/run-tests.sh with shellcheck installed; the suite skips that pass
  when it is missing, so a local green is weaker than CI's.

## Comments

Comments here explain why, especially why something that looks wrong is
deliberate. Several encode a specific past incident. Do not strip or "tidy"
them; write in the same register.

## Testing reality

build_files/build.sh, build_files/kernel-akmods.sh, build_files/zfs.sh and the
Containerfile only execute inside an image build. Nothing on the host reaches
them, so a green suite is not evidence for a change to any of them. post-check.sh
is partly covered through its sourceable helpers. State how an image-build
change was verified, or that it was not.
